1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,707
The room feels cool thanks to

2
00:00:02,747 --> 00:00:04,652
the air conditioner, or AC.

3
00:00:05,182 --> 00:00:07,272
But where does the cold actually come from?

4
00:00:08,652 --> 00:00:10,360
Heat is energy that moves because

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,884
of a temperature difference.

6
00:00:12,414 --> 00:00:14,382
An AC does not create cold.

7
00:00:14,912 --> 00:00:16,343
It moves heat from inside

8
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:17,796
the room to the outside.

9
00:00:19,176 --> 00:00:21,828
An AC cycle has four components:

10
00:00:21,868 --> 00:00:23,090
the compressor,

11
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:26,747
condenser, expansion valve, and evaporator.

12
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:30,061
The refrigerant, the working fluid,

13
00:00:30,101 --> 00:00:31,957
flows through all four.

14
00:00:33,337 --> 00:00:35,535
First, low-pressure refrigerant

15
00:00:35,575 --> 00:00:37,597
vapor enters the compressor.

16
00:00:38,127 --> 00:00:39,762
The compressor raises the vapor's

17
00:00:39,802 --> 00:00:41,630
pressure and temperature using work.

18
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:44,732
Second, the hot vapor flows to

19
00:00:44,772 --> 00:00:46,768
the condenser in the outdoor unit.

20
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:49,190
The vapor releases heat to the outside

21
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:50,857
air and condenses into a liquid.

22
00:00:52,237 --> 00:00:53,758
Third, the liquid passes

23
00:00:53,798 --> 00:00:55,620
through the expansion valve.

24
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:58,223
Pressure drops, and the refrigerant

25
00:00:58,263 --> 00:01:00,858
becomes a cold mixture of liquid and vapor.

26
00:01:02,238 --> 00:01:04,409
Fourth, that cold mixture enters

27
00:01:04,449 --> 00:01:06,591
the evaporator inside the room.

28
00:01:07,121 --> 00:01:09,413
It absorbs heat from the room air,

29
00:01:09,453 --> 00:01:10,551
then evaporates.

30
00:01:11,931 --> 00:01:13,920
The vapor returns to the compressor,

31
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,200
and the cycle repeats.

32
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:17,738
Heat keeps being absorbed inside and

33
00:01:17,778 --> 00:01:20,110
released outside, so the room stays cool.

34
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:23,063
Heat does not flow by itself

35
00:01:23,103 --> 00:01:25,004
from a cold place to a hot place.

36
00:01:25,534 --> 00:01:27,922
That is why the compressor needs work.

37
00:01:29,302 --> 00:01:31,665
The measure of an AC's performance is called

38
00:01:31,705 --> 00:01:33,835
the coefficient of performance, or COP.

39
00:01:34,365 --> 00:01:36,161
Its value is the heat absorbed

40
00:01:36,201 --> 00:01:38,098
divided by the compressor work.

41
00:01:39,478 --> 00:01:41,463
So, the compressor squeezes,

42
00:01:41,503 --> 00:01:43,488
the condenser releases heat,

43
00:01:43,528 --> 00:01:45,369
the valve lowers pressure,

44
00:01:45,409 --> 00:01:47,723
and the evaporator absorbs heat.

45
00:01:49,103 --> 00:01:50,788
Want to understand machines

46
00:01:50,828 --> 00:01:52,234
like this more deeply?

47
00:01:52,764 --> 00:01:55,050
Come study Mechanical Engineering at

48
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:57,417
Universitas Muhammadiyah Yogyakarta.
